  "verdict": "CONFIRMED. Every Encore-forced and Struggle-forced opponent action draws >= 1 Random() in HandleAction_UseMove's own frame (1, 2, 1, 1, 3 across the five such actions recorded); every one of the control arm's eight ordinary chosen-move prologues draws exactly 0. The counts are geometric (p = 1/2 with gBattlersCount = 2), visible within a single arm (seed 305419897: 1 then 2) and across seeds (seed 1234567890: 1 then 1; struggle arm: 1 then 3).",
  "engineDivergence": {
    "kernel": "src/engine/factoryBattleScriptFullTurnDecision.ts (UNFIXED, at this commit)",
    "getMoveTargetDrawsOnAllFourBranches": 0,
    "derivation": "sourceMoveTarget (:1959-1987) is a pure switch over the generated target shape and takes no RNG argument -- its own docstring (:1951-1958) asserts 'every non-user shape resolves ... without consuming RNG', which is correct for DEPENDS/BOTH/FOES_AND_ALLY/OPPONENTS_FIELD/RANDOM in singles and WRONG for MOVE_TARGET_SELECTED. Its three callers -- legalMoveDecisions' forced-Struggle arm (:2013), its ordinary arm (:2022) and lockedMoveDecision's Encore arm (:2184) -- all run at decision-listing time, and buildActionContext (:1489-1523) draws nothing on the action path. The port therefore spends 0 draws where the ROM spends 1, 2, 1, 1 and 3 above.",
    "modeledElsewhere": "battleScriptSwitchinOpcode.ts:1036-1058 already runs this exact do/while for Cmd_various VARIOUS_GET_MOVE_TARGET; it is simply not wired to the four HandleAction_UseMove branches.",
    "executableConfirmation": "tests/issue140GetMoveTargetReceipt.test.ts (added with the fix; its mutation-check removes the loop and the arm counts go back to 0)"
  }
